Subject: ntdll: widen the vprot tracer to the game's own code pages

The tracer added alongside the segv one only logged VirtualProtect calls in the
32-bit builtin range, because the question then was who made user32's code
writable. That question is answered -- the overlay did, and the calls succeeded.

The remaining one is a floor lower and outside that range. Valve's CEG DRM
decrypts and checksums the game's OWN code before it will run; when the check
fails the game prints "In memory integrity check failed. This may be caused by
debug breakpoints or DLL relocation." and exits(3). All of that happens at the
image base -- 0x400000 for this 32-bit exe -- which the filter excluded. So the
log showing nothing for the DRM was not evidence that the DRM did nothing.

Filter on EXECUTE protection rather than on a second address range: it catches
code-page manipulation wherever an image lands, without readmitting the heap and
data churn that makes VirtualProtect one of the busiest calls at startup. Cap
raised 256 -> 1024 accordingly.

The blunt alternative was tried first and does not work: WINEDEBUG=+virtual
cannot be scoped to the game, because the game inherits its environment from
Steam, so it instruments the whole Steam process tree. It wrote 53 MB in under a
minute and left Steam with no window -- which is also the signature of a separate
open bug, so it destroys the very thing it was meant to observe.

Refines the tracer from the fault-diagnostics patch and drops with it.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 74a4eea4000..4ceeea14b2d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5841,7 +5841,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtFreeVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SIZE_T *si
 }
 
 
-/* ---- VPROT-TRACE (temporary): who asks to make a builtin's code writable? ----
+/* ---- VPROT-TRACE (temporary): who asks to make CODE writable? ---------------
  * Something writes into user32's GetAsyncKeyState thunk (confirmed: base
  * 0x7b8e0000 + 0xa430) on a page Wine keeps r-x, and the resulting
  * EXC_BAD_ACCESS is swallowed by Rosetta's exception server and retried
@@ -5853,18 +5853,34 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtFreeVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SIZE_T *si
  *   - no call at all means the writer never asked, and would have faulted on
  *     Windows too -- so the difference is elsewhere.
  *
- * Only calls touching the 32-bit builtin range are logged. VirtualProtect runs
- * constantly during startup and an unfiltered log would both bury the one call
- * that matters and perturb the timing of the thing being measured.
+ * Two filters, because there are two questions. The builtin range answers the
+ * original one above. The executable-protection filter answers the second:
+ * Valve's CEG DRM decrypts and checksums the game's OWN code, and when it fails
+ * the game prints "In memory integrity check failed. This may be caused by debug
+ * breakpoints or DLL relocation." and exits(3). That work happens at the image
+ * base (0x400000 for a 32-bit exe), which the builtin filter excluded -- so the
+ * log showing nothing there was never evidence that nothing happened.
+ *
+ * Filtering on EXECUTE rather than on an address range keeps this usable: it
+ * catches code-page manipulation wherever the image landed, while leaving out
+ * the heap and data churn that makes VirtualProtect one of the busiest calls
+ * during startup. An unfiltered log would bury the calls that matter and perturb
+ * the timing of the thing being measured -- WINEDEBUG=+virtual was tried and
+ * wrote 53 MB in under a minute, which is not a measurement, it is a load test.
+ *
  * Shares WINE_SEGV_TRACE's switch. Remove after use. */
+#define VPROT_TRACE_EXEC (PAGE_EXECUTE | PAGE_EXECUTE_READ | \
+                          PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE | PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY)
 static void vprot_note( const void *addr, SIZE_T size, ULONG new_prot, ULONG old, unsigned int status )
 {
-    static int fd = -1, checked, left = 256;
+    static int fd = -1, checked, left = 1024;
     char line[256];
     ULONG_PTR a = (ULONG_PTR)addr;
     int len;
 
-    if ((a + size) < 0x7b000000 || a >= 0x7c000000) return;
+    if (((a + size) < 0x7b000000 || a >= 0x7c000000) &&
+        !(new_prot & VPROT_TRACE_EXEC) && !(old & VPROT_TRACE_EXEC))
+        return;
 
     if (!checked)
     {
